Office hours have ended, and we look outside through the window.
It is raining very heavily outside.
Water has completely pooled on the streets.
Because of the rain, the buses are running very late.
Rohan says, "Maya, today we will not get a bus."
Priya suggests, "We should go by the metro."
So, the three of us walk to the nearby metro station.
We enter the station, and there is a huge crowd there.
A few months ago, I used the metro for the first time.
At that time, I felt a little scared of the crowd.
But now, this journey has become very easy for me.
I easily scan my card at the gate.
The train has arrived on time on the platform.
We go inside, and we get a place to sit.
Priya says, "It rained a lot yesterday too."
Rohan laughs and says, "But today the monsoon has broken all records."
We sit comfortably and chat about my birthday.
The metro takes us quickly towards my building.
There is a lot of rain outside, but I have now learned to travel in this city.
